# FOAM mobile security

## Real authorization

Client-side checks are UX only.

Enforce authorization with:

- Firebase Security Rules
- Cloud Functions
- existing server-side authorization mechanisms

Never treat these as the security boundary:

- hidden UI buttons
- client state / local storage / local role flags
- navigation guards alone

## Privileges & credentials

- Never put privileged credentials in the mobile app
- Do not weaken Firebase rules to make mobile easier
- Do not bypass existing staff authorization
- Staff roles/access must follow the existing FOAM authorization model

If mobile work needs a backend authorization change: **STOP** and request explicit approval.

## Logging

Never log: passwords, tokens, private keys, authentication credentials, or sensitive customer information unnecessarily.
